+  // On some pages (confirmed on the homepage, with content that appears to
+  // re-render/hydrate shortly after first paint) the search plugin's own
+  // click/keydown handlers never end up attached to the button/input that's
+  // actually in the DOM by the time a user interacts with it — its setup
+  // runs once, on the router's very first "nav" notification, and if
+  // anything in the page replaces that markup afterward the freshly
+  // rendered elements are left listener-less until a real in-app
+  // navigation triggers "nav" again (confirmed this reproduces identically
+  // against the stock, unmodified plugin — not something introduced by the
+  // other customizations in this file). Firing one supplementary "nav"
+  // event after window "load" (later than DOMContentLoaded, by which point
+  // any such re-render has settled) gives it a second, final setup pass on
